                        "language": "english",
                        "review": "I played this game for a little while as it looked like a really interesting idea.\n\nThe developer is ambitious, but as it stands now, I can't suggest getting it for $15.  Here are some of the issues I had in the first 15 minutes.\n\n-If you aren't holding something, you can't see your hands, makes interaction a bit harder\n-The quests seem to reset randomly, and there is no way to save beyond the auto-save.\n-There is no tutorial, you have to figure out everything through a lot of trial and error\n-There is no quest markers or indicators, you just have to wander around until you find where you are supposed to go.\n-Combat is a tad dry.\n-Had a lot of issues picking up objects, as they would suddenly melt into the ground.\n-Game lags even on low settings with a high end machine.\n\nThat being said...  This game looks like it could be really, really, really cool.  But a lot of the basics are missing, and really take away from the experience.  It is a single developer and they seem to be very responsive, so I have no doubt things will quickly improve.  But as of right now, it has a lot of issues with the bare bones of the game.",
